name=say
category=system
description=print text with optional backslash escape translation
usage=say [-e|--escapes] [--] [text ...]
option=-h, --help    show this help
option=-e, --escapes translate supported backslash escapes before writing
note=Supports \\, \n, \r, \t, and \e; unknown and trailing escapes stay literal.
note=Without -e, backslashes stay literal. Redirected output receives emitted bytes unchanged.
note=Example: say -e '\e{fg:b_green}Success!\e{ok}'
